quence but the main serine-generating steps are unbalanced. Literature suggests formose chemistry is unselective and serine yield is low. Major feasibility deficit comes from rxn_003 and rxn_004 conservation errors as above. Pathway is correct in concept but incomplete in mechanistic and mass/charge detail.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\n                \"rxn_003\",\n                \"rxn_004\"\n            ],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Update all reactions for mass and charge balance.\",\n                \"Model competing formose products and side reactions as per literature.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_008\": 0.3,\n                \"rxn_007\": 0.7,\n                \"rxn_005\": 0.0\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.35,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.7,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.85,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.4,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.45,\n            \"feedback\": \"This pathway relies on aminoacetonitrile and glycine as intermediates for serine synthesis via Strecker/aldol logic. Both rxn_008 (unbalanced) and rxn_007 (needs missing H2O or other) violate conservation, and rxn_005 (hydroxymethylation producing serine + hydroxymethylserine) is unbalanced and stoichiometrically unclear. Literature support is partial (copper-catalysed aldol and Strecker both established, but not jointly to serine in this way).\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\n                \"rxn_008\",\n                \"rxn_007\",\n                \"rxn_005\"\n            ],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Balance NH3/C/N units in Strecker steps and aldol.\",\n                \"Clarify glycine hydroxymethylation mechanism and products.\",\n                \"Add explicit copper/metal catalysis to reflect Akabori conditions.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_005\": 0.0\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.0,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.2,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.7,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.2,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.2,\n            \"feedback\": \"Despite solid literature precedent for copper-catalysed glycine + HCHO \u2192 serine (Akabori reaction), rxn_005 is unbalanced: three carbons, three nitrogens and two oxygens are unaccounted for as written; coproduct stoichiometry is wrong. This step requires review and addition of missing products (water, ammonia, etc.) to match mass and charge conservation. Current form violates basic chemistry.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\n                \"rxn_005\"\n            ],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Balance all atoms in glycine + formaldehyde \u2192 serine (+ expected hydroxymethylserine, water, etc.) and include catalyst explicitly.\",\n                \"If coproduct is hydroxymethylserine, specify the full structure and stoichiometry.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_011\": 0.7,\n                \"rxn_010\": 0.4\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.3,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.7,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.85,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.3,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.3,\n            \"feedback\": \"The biomimetic pathway via hydroxypyruvate is highly speculative; literature finds no experimental demonstration that hydroxypyruvate can be aminated to serine prebiotically. rxn_010 is unbalanced by +2 hydrogens, needing H2 or another byproduct for conservation. This path should be marked 'untested hypothesis,' not an established prebiotic route.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\n                \"rxn_010\"\n            ],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Flag this route as speculative/untested.\",\n                \"Improve atom balancing, clearly stating missing byproducts (H2, H2O, etc.).\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_012\": 0.5\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.4,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.6,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.8,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.35,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.45,\n            \"feedback\": \"Polyglycine surface hydroxymethylation is only weakly supported in modern replication and rxn_012 is underdefined (unclear whether it refers to polyglycine or free glycine, and confirmation of side products is lacking). The reaction is not balanced; insufficient detail on mechanism and stoichiometry reduces the pathway's reliability.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\n                \"rxn_012\"\n            ],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Expand description to specify polymer context, surface chemistry, and all byproducts.\",\n                \"Add modern literature support if available.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_014\": 0.2\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.2,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.35,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.7,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.2,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.25,\n            \"feedback\": \"The interstellar/parent-body environment can yield serine, but rxn_014 is unbalanced (C, H, O, N), and yields are low and ill-defined per literature. Key intermediates and byproducts omitted. This pathway should be demoted to 'possible but minor' contribution with much clearer stoichiometry.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\n                \"rxn_014\"\n            ],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Add water, CO2, or other species as necessary to balance reaction.\",\n                \"Include irradiation/hydrolysis context from literature and clarify expected side products.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P9\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_015\": 0.2\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.2,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.4,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.8,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.2,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.25,\n            \"feedback\": \"Spark discharge experiments do yield serine alongside numerous other products, but rxn_015 is unbalanced (missing CO2/O2, improperly matches elemental count). Should be included as a low-yield, unselective background route only, not a main contributor.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\n                \"rxn_015\"\n            ],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Balance full atom content (likely needing CO2 or O2 as product or reactant).\",\n                \"Cite actual yield as fraction of glycine/alanine from Johnson et al. (2008) if available.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P10\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_013\": 0.8\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.7,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.65,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.85,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.7,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.75,\n            \"feedback\": \"Serine retro-aldol/\u03b2-elimination to