doxal/metal-catalysed serine synthesis, which is robust in vitro (Metzler & Snell), and uses realistic environmental/catalytic conditions. The main weakness is that prebiotic plausibility for abundant pyridoxal is lower, but the chemistry is demonstrated. Ensure full mass balancing for the step, especially for water and reversible byproducts.", "approved": true, "problematic_reactions": [], "suggestions": ["Balance reaction fully and consider addition of pyridoxal/Schiff base intermediates.", "Cite potential reversibility and product inhibition if applicable."]}, {"pathway_id": "P5", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_007": 0.8}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.8, "pathway_coherence": 0.89, "environmental_progression": 0.9, "target_achievement": 1.0, "overall_confidence": 0.87, "feedback": "Polyglycine side-chain hydroxymethylation (Akabori, Okawa & Sato 1956) is plausible, if speculative. The chemistry is documented as possible on kaolinite, but the net reaction would benefit from full atom balance and explicit coverage of competing side reactions (over-alkylation). There is little modern quantitative data, so this pathway cannot score as highly as demonstrated ones.", "approved": true, "problematic_reactions": [], "suggestions": ["Fully balance reactants and products including all water and over-alkylated intermediates.", "Flag pathway as speculative, as yields and rates are unquantified in the literature."]}, {"pathway_id": "P6", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_009": 0.6, "rxn_010": 0.9}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.7, "pathway_coherence": 0.8, "environmental_progression": 0.9, "target_achievement": 1.0, "overall_confidence": 0.82, "feedback": "Hydrothermal Strecker synthesis is viable but the Strecker reaction (rxn_009) is flagged as atom UNBALANCED (missing C, surplus H), mirroring issues in the surface Strecker step. Reports of transient serine production are experimentally confirmed, but serine rapidly degrades at such temperatures, so this is not a net-productive route. Hydrolysis s