roved": true, "problematic_reactions": [], "suggestions": ["Clarify in network notes that net serine yields are low relative to glycine and unselective mixtures dominate."]}, {"pathway_id": "P9", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_014": 0.9}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.9, "pathway_coherence": 0.9, "environmental_progression": 0.95, "target_achievement": 1.0, "overall_confidence": 0.94, "feedback": "UV-irradiation/photolytic synthesis in ices or parent bodies is literature-supported and routinely yields serine (Bernstein et al., Mu\u00f1oz Caro et al.). The yield is low and often only after acid hydrolysis. Chemical feasibility is fine as a gross process but quantitative details and atom balances for intermediates/byproducts are not resolved. Reaction is balanceable. Environmental conditions are reflected accurately.", "approved": true, "problematic_reactions": [], "suggestions": ["Annotate expected yield as low and resulting from complex, nonselective chemistry.", "Indicate post-irradiation hydrolysis is often necessary for free serine detection."]}, {"pathway_id": "P10", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_015": 0.85, "rxn_016": 0.85}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.85, "pathway_coherence": 0.92, "environmental_progression": 0.95, "target_achievement": 1.0, "overall_confidence": 0.92, "feedback": "Retro-aldol and \u03b2-elimination linkages are chemically and mechanistically well-supported (Metzler & Snell, Ter-Ovanessian), reflecting serine's known lability under aqueous and thermal conditions. Reaction stoichiometry appears reasonable but should be balance-checked. This is correctly depicted as a degradation/sink path rather than a productive route.", "approved": true, "problematic_reactions": [], "suggestions": ["Balance both degradation steps fully.", "Model competitive kinetics and net serine loss where relevant."]}], "best_pathway_id": "P3", "overall_confidence": 0.88, "network_feedback": "This network presents a comprehensive, multi-pathway synthesis of prebiotic serine, capturing all